Directory: /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_007/backend

Requirements:
1. Create venv virtual environment, requirements.txt with: fastapi, uvicorn, sqlalchemy, pydantic, python-dotenv
2. Create app/ with proper package structure (__init__.py files)
3. database.py - SQLite database connection using SQLAlchemy 2.0
4. models.py - Category, Transaction, Budget ORM models per architecture doc
5. schemas.py - Pydantic request/response schemas
6. routers/categories.py - CRUD for categories with query filtering by type
7. routers/transactions.py - CRUD for transactions with pagination (page/page_size), month filtering, category_id filtering. Amount stored as float (positive for income, negative for expense).
8. routers/budgets.py - CRUD for budgets per category per month
9. routers/dashboard.py - Four endpoints:
   - /api/dashboard/summary?month=YYYY-MM -> total_income, total_expense, balance
   - /api/dashboard/expense-pie?month=YYYY-MM -> [{category, amount, percentage}]
   - /api/dashboard/monthly-trend?months=N -> [{month, income, expense}]
   - /api/dashboard/budget-alerts?month=YYYY-MM -> [{category, budget, spent, excess}]
10. seed.py - Insert preset categories on startup if DB empty
11. main.py - FastAPI app with CORS (allow localhost:3000), include all routers, run seed on startup
12. run.py - simple script to uvicorn.run(app, host='0.0.0.0', port=8000)

IMPORTANT: Use positive amounts for income and positive amounts for expenses (distinguish by category type). Make sure all APIs work correctly.

Create ALL files needed for a fully functional backend.
  ○ [p3_frontend] Implement Next.js frontend
    agent:  Frontend Developer (programmer_2)
    desc:   Read the architecture document at /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_007/program_architecture.md first, then implement the complete Next.js frontend.

Directory: /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_007/frontend

Requirements:
1. Initialize a Next.js 14+ project with App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
2. Set up Shadcn UI (npx shadcn-ui@latest init, add button, card, dialog, input, select, table, badge, alert components)
3. Install recharts and axios
4. Create src/types/index.ts with TypeScript interfaces:
   - Category {id, name, type, icon?}
   - Transaction {id, category_id, category_name?, amount, date, note?}
   - Budget {id, category_id, category_name?, month, amount}
   - SummaryData {total_income, total_expense, balance, month}
   - PieData {category, amount, percentage}
   - TrendData {month, income, expense}
   - BudgetAlert {category, budget, spent, excess}
5. Create src/lib/api.ts with Axios instance (baseURL: http://localhost:8000/api) and all API functions
6. Create sidebar navigation component with links to Dashboard, Transactions, Categories, Budgets
7. Create src/app/layout.tsx with sidebar layout
8. Dashboard page (src/app/page.tsx):
   - SummaryCards showing total_income, total_expense, balance
   - ExpensePieChart using Recharts PieChart
   - MonthlyTrendChart using Recharts LineChart
   - BudgetAlert list
9. Transactions page (src/app/transactions/page.tsx):
   - Table with all transactions
   - Month filter (select or input type=month)
   - Pagination
   - Add/Edit/Delete via dialog forms
10. Categories page (src/app/categories/page.tsx):
    - List grouped by type (income/expense)
    - Add/Edit/Delete via dialog forms
11. Budgets page (src/app/budgets/page.tsx):
    - Table with each expense category, budget amount, spent amount
    - Highlight in red when spent > budget
    - Edit budget via dialog
12. Create a proper globals.css with Tailwind directives

Make sure the frontend compiles and all pages have proper error handling. Use 'use client' where needed for interactive components.
