## Types from @/types:
Transaction { id: number; category_id: number; category_name?: string; amount: number; date: string; note?: string; }
Category { id: number; name: string; type: 'income' | 'expense'; icon?: string; }

## API functions from @/lib/api.ts:
fetchCategories(type?: string): Promise<Category[]>
fetchTransactions(params?: FetchTransactionsParams): Promise<PaginatedTransactions>
createTransaction(data: Omit<Transaction, 'id'>): Promise<Transaction>
updateTransaction(id: number, data: Partial<Transaction>): Promise<Transaction>
deleteTransaction(id: number): Promise<void>

Where:
interface FetchTransactionsParams { month?: string; page?: number; per_page?: number; category_id?: number; }
interface PaginatedTransactions { items: Transaction[]; total: number; page: number; per_page: number; total_pages: number; }

## Requirements
1. Month filter at top - a text input type="month" (default: current month as YYYY-MM)
2. "Add Transaction" button opens a modal/form
3. Transaction form fields:
   - category_id: select dropdown (fetch categories, group by type with optgroup)
   - amount: number input (required, positive)
   - date: date input (default today)
   - note: text input (optional)
4. Transactions displayed in a table with columns: Date, Category, Amount, Note, Actions
5. Income amounts shown in green, expense amounts shown in red
6. Pagination at bottom: "Previous" and "Next" buttons, showing "Page X of Y"
7. Each row has Edit and Delete buttons
8. Edit opens the same form pre-filled with existing values
9. Delete confirms via window.confirm
10. Handle loading and error states
11. Use tailwind styling only (no shadcn)
12. Date filter change + pagination should re-fetch data

