This is a client-side React page ('use client') for managing monthly budgets with alerts when spending exceeds budget.

## Context
- The sidebar already links to '/budgets'
- The layout wraps pages with Sidebar + main content area
- Dashboard reference page: /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_007/frontend/src/app/page.tsx

## Types from @/types:
Budget { id: number; category_id: number; category_name?: string; month: string; amount: number; }
Category { id: number; name: string; type: 'income' | 'expense'; icon?: string; }
BudgetAlert { category: string; budget: number; spent: number; excess: number; }

## API functions from @/lib/api.ts:
fetchCategories(type?: string): Promise<Category[]>
fetchBudgets(month?: string): Promise<Budget[]>
createBudget(data: Omit<Budget, 'id'>): Promise<Budget>
updateBudget(id: number, data: Partial<Budget>): Promise<Budget>
deleteBudget(id: number): Promise<void>

## Dashboard summary API (for budget alert data):
fetchSummary(month?: string) returns: SummaryData { total_income, total_expense, balance, month }

## Requirements
1. Month filter at top - text input type="month" (default: current month as YYYY-MM)
2. Display a list of expense categories with their budget vs. actual spending
   - For each expense category: show category name, budget amount, spent amount, progress bar, remaining
   - If spent > budget, show the row with RED background and a warning badge showing overspend amount
   - Progress bar: green if under budget, red if over budget
3. For categories WITHOUT a budget set, show a "Set Budget" button
4. "Set Budget" or "Edit Budget" opens an inline form with:
   - category_id: select dropdown (only expense categories)
   - amount: number input (required, positive)
   - month: hidden (uses the currently selected month)
5. Each budget row has Edit and Delete buttons
6. At the top, show a summary alert section: if any budgets are exceeded, show a red alert card listing them
7. Handle loading and error states
8. Use tailwind styling only (no shadcn)

